<section class="legacy-consolidations" id="consolidated-legacy-evidence"><h2>MINI diagnostic app compatibility: original source findings</h2><p>Instead of keeping an overlapping URL for every similar product or protocol permutation, these source-specific findings and original research diagrams are now integrated into the matching canonical reference. Each historical public URL redirects to its evidence anchor; original Markdown remains accessible to editors in Git history.</p><article class="legacy-case" id="mini-diagnostic-app"><h3>'MINI Diagnostic App: Choose by Diagnosis, Service, and Adapter Fit'</h3><p class="legacy-provenance">Original independent comparison at <code>/guides/mini-diagnostic-app/</code> has been merged here with a direct 301. This subsection retains its independently useful distinctions.</p><h4>Shortlist by documented role</h4><p>This is a current official-claim comparison, not a hands-on ranking. A category does not mean every module, parameter or procedure exists on every MINI.</p><h4>Match jobs to evidence</h4><p>For a warning light, demand exact module diagnostics and code coverage. For live investigation, demand named parameters or module data. For battery registration, service reset or parking-brake work, demand the exact function and vehicle. For personalization, use a coding-specific options record rather than assuming a diagnostic license includes coding.</p><h4>Buying sequence</h4><p>1. Record MINI model, generation, production year and equipment. 2. Name the module, data, service function or coding option. 3. Check exact vehicle/function on the current official app page. 4. Check supported adapter, connection method and iOS/Android requirement. 5. Record whether the license is one-time, platform-specific, annual or bundled with hardware. 6. Buy only after every row is confirmed; a return policy is not compatibility evidence.</p><details><summary>Original diagrams (2)</summary><figure><picture><source media="(max-width:640px)" srcset=